  "preamble": "Lateralization of the rhotic approximant [ɹ] to [l]. Proto-Iroquoian is reconstructed with an approximant *ɹ, which Proto-Northern-Iroquoian kept as a rhotic, while Cherokee, the Southern Iroquoian language, has l in its place: *-tsiːɹ 'fire' > atsila, *kuːɹeh 'acorn' > gule.",
